TEXT 160 -80 Left 3 ;#381 Twin-tee oscillator trimmed for lowest distortion
TEXT 160 -16 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dm1YjETg3rU
TEXT 160 32 Left 2 ;Trimming the shunt leg sets how much gain the notch leaves in the loop. Too much and the sine compresses against the rails.
TEXT 160 936 Left 2 !.lib LTC.lib
TEXT 160 976 Left 2 !.ic V(out)=3.5
TEXT 160 1016 Left 2 !.tran 0 5s 4.7s 1u uic
TEXT 160 1056 Left 2 !.step param TRIM list 200 250 295 300
TEXT 160 1096 Left 2 !.four 1.592k V(out)
TEXT 160 1136 Left 2 !.meas tran AMP_EARLY PP V(out) FROM 4.70s TO 4.72s
TEXT 160 1176 Left 2 !.meas tran AMP_LATE PP V(out) FROM 4.98s TO 5s
TEXT 160 1216 Left 2 !.meas tran VMAX MAX V(out) FROM 4.98s TO 5s
TEXT 160 1256 Left 2 !.meas tran VMIN MIN V(out) FROM 4.98s TO 5s
TEXT 160 1296 Left 2 !.meas tran PERIOD TRIG V(out)=2.37 RISE=10 TARG V(out)=2.37 RISE=20
TEXT 160 1336 Left 2 !.meas tran FREQ PARAM 10/PERIOD
TEXT 160 1376 Left 2 !.meas tran HOLD PARAM AMP_LATE/AMP_EARLY
TEXT 160 1416 Left 2 !.save V(out)
TEXT 160 1480 Left 2 ;RTRIM stands for the wiper setting of the 500 ohm trim pot Alan draws in series with the 4.7k shunt leg; his knob position is never shown.
TEXT 160 1520 Left 2 ;U1 is an LT1810, the rail-to-rail input and output part from LTspice's own LTC.lib. Alan's drawing calls for an MCP6002 "or any R-R I/O op amp".
